# Every pattern here is `**/`-prefixed: Docker matches a slash-less pattern only at the context
# root, so a bare `coverage` or `.claude` would let a nested one into the image. That is how
# apps/backend/.env used to get in while .gitignore hid it from `git status`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.git
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
**/.playwright-mcp
**/.codegraph
**/.claude
